  "details": "UDONSDK-2020.01.14.10.47_Public\nVRCSDK3-2020.01.14.10.40\nDescription:\nIf you add a node without moving  its position, the node can snap to what I believe is the origin of the graph when you select a new input type. When you can't see the position change in larger graphs it may appear to some as if the node just deletes itself.\nSteps to reproduce:\n1. Add any node that allows input changes from the drop down. In my example I used the vector3 constructor node.\n2. Without moving the node, change the type from (float, float) to (float, float, float).\nExample:",
